From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:49:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: Go back to the other vboot slot from the
 setup

[ouroBIOS: patches/edk2/0020, without the files that TianoCore's tree
does not have (tools/edk2-import.py): 7 in edk2/OuroBiosPkg (3 in a
directory of TianoCore's that the package carries whole)]

With coreboot's vboot and two RW slots, an update capsule writes the slot
that does not run and boots it; the other slot keeps the release before,
until the next update. Going back to it needed an OS: tools/update.py
rollback stages the capsule of that release, which the firmware finds
already written, so that it only asks vboot to try that slot.

coreboot's SMMSTORE handler now does that on request
(SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_TRY_OTHER), and refuses it until the next boot after
SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_LOCK. Add both to SmmStoreLib. PlatformBootManagerLib
sends the lock when a boot option starts (ReadyToBoot, which booting the
setup does not signal) and at ExitBootServices(), or at once if it cannot
wait for those: an OS loader, the UEFI Shell or an OS cannot go back to an
older release without the checks of a capsule.

The Firmware Update page shows the slot that runs (the one of the CBFS
that coreboot reports) and the release in each slot: COREBOOT_EXTRA_VERSION
of the "revision" file in the CBFS of the slot, read through the flash
window. "Go back to <release>" asks for a confirmation and restarts into
the other slot, after the checks of a capsule that can be made here: a
release that is not the one that runs, of the same variant (mrc or nri,
whose cache-as-RAM layouts differ, or fsp on the M920x; both must be
known), with a version not
older than the lowest supported one. vboot checks the signature of the
slot at the next boot, and comes back if it does not verify or does not
boot twice.

TEST=tools/qemu-update.py of ouroBIOS at every build: from the setup of
ROM D, "Go back to" the release of B (keys sent by QEMU, the pages
followed on the serial port) switches the slot without writing it;
tools/efi/slot-lock-test.c started from the ESP is refused before and
after ExitBootServices(); the page shows the slots and the release in
each.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv

---
diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/Include/Guid/FirmwareUpdateConfig.h b/UefiPayloadPkg/Include/Guid/FirmwareUpdateConfig.h
index 68939a0c4..67857457a 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Include/Guid/FirmwareUpdateConfig.h
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Include/Guid/FirmwareUpdateConfig.h
@@ -14,5 +14,6 @@
 
 #define FIRMWARE_UPDATE_FORM_ID              0x1000
 #define FIRMWARE_UPDATE_INSTALL_QUESTION_ID  0x1001
+#define FIRMWARE_UPDATE_SLOT_QUESTION_ID     0x1002
 
 #endif
diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/Include/Library/SmmStoreLib.h b/UefiPayloadPkg/Include/Library/SmmStoreLib.h
index fab6c3385..3b7d054ab 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Include/Library/SmmStoreLib.h
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Include/Library/SmmStoreLib.h
@@ -175,6 +175,42 @@ SmmStoreLibVbootSlotGood (
   VOID
   );
 
+/**
+  Ask coreboot to boot the RW slot that is not running from the next boot:
+  vboot tries it twice, as after an update, and comes back to the slot that
+  runs now if it does not boot.  coreboot also clears the memory training
+  cache, which that slot must not reuse.
+
+  @retval EFI_SUCCESS       vboot tries the other slot at the next boot.
+  @retval EFI_NO_MEDIA      SmmStore is not initialized.
+  @retval EFI_UNSUPPORTED   coreboot has no two RW slots with the vboot nvdata
+                            in flash.
+  @retval others            The handler refused: locked until the next boot,
+                            or no valid nvdata.
+
+**/
+EFI_STATUS
+SmmStoreLibVbootTryOtherSlot (
+  VOID
+  );
+
+/**
+  Make coreboot refuse SmmStoreLibVbootTryOtherSlot() until the next boot.
+  To be called before a boot option or an OS starts.  Allocates nothing: it
+  can be called from ExitBootServices().
+
+  @retval EFI_SUCCESS       Refused until the next boot.
+  @retval EFI_NO_MEDIA      SmmStore is not initialized.
+  @retval EFI_UNSUPPORTED   coreboot has no two RW slots with the vboot nvdata
+                            in flash: nothing to refuse.
+  @retval others            The handler failed.
+
+**/
+EFI_STATUS
+SmmStoreLibVbootLockSlots (
+  VOID
+  );
+
 /**
   Function to update a pointer on virtual address change.  Matches the signature
   and operation of EfiConvertPointer.
diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/SmmStoreLib/SmmStore.c b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/SmmStoreLib/SmmStore.c
index e7a6b73c7..98f282b82 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/SmmStoreLib/SmmStore.c
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/SmmStoreLib/SmmStore.c
@@ -430,6 +430,56 @@ SmmStoreLibVbootSlotGood (
   return CallSmm (mSmmStoreInfo->ApmCmd, SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_SLOT_GOOD, mArgComBufPhys);
 }
 
+/**
+  Ask coreboot to boot the RW slot that is not running from the next boot:
+  vboot tries it twice, as after an update, and comes back to the slot that
+  runs now if it does not boot.  coreboot also clears the memory training
+  cache, which that slot must not reuse.
+
+  @retval EFI_SUCCESS       vboot tries the other slot at the next boot.
+  @retval EFI_NO_MEDIA      SmmStore is not initialized.
+  @retval EFI_UNSUPPORTED   coreboot has no two RW slots with the vboot nvdata
+                            in flash.
+  @retval others            The handler refused: locked until the next boot,
+                            or no valid nvdata.
+
+**/
+EFI_STATUS
+SmmStoreLibVbootTryOtherSlot (
+  VOID
+  )
+{
+  if (mSmmStoreInfo == NULL) {
+    return EFI_NO_MEDIA;
+  }
+
+  return CallSmm (mSmmStoreInfo->ApmCmd, SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_TRY_OTHER, mArgComBufPhys);
+}
+
+/**
+  Make coreboot refuse SmmStoreLibVbootTryOtherSlot() until the next boot.
+  To be called before a boot option or an OS starts.  Allocates nothing: it
+  can be called from ExitBootServices().
+
+  @retval EFI_SUCCESS       Refused until the next boot.
+  @retval EFI_NO_MEDIA      SmmStore is not initialized.
+  @retval EFI_UNSUPPORTED   coreboot has no two RW slots with the vboot nvdata
+                            in flash: nothing to refuse.
+  @retval others            The handler failed.
+
+**/
+EFI_STATUS
+SmmStoreLibVbootLockSlots (
+  VOID
+  )
+{
+  if (mSmmStoreInfo == NULL) {
+    return EFI_NO_MEDIA;
+  }
+
+  return CallSmm (mSmmStoreInfo->ApmCmd, SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_LOCK, mArgComBufPhys);
+}
+
 /**
   Fixup internal data so that EFI can be called in virtual mode.
   Converts any pointers in lib to virtual mode. This function is meant to
diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/SmmStoreLib/SmmStore.h b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/SmmStoreLib/SmmStore.h
index 2e78cc89e..f899b5dca 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/SmmStoreLib/SmmStore.h
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/SmmStoreLib/SmmStore.h
@@ -24,6 +24,13 @@
 //
 #define SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_SLOT_GOOD  8
 
+//
+// coreboot with vboot and two RW slots: try the slot that is not running at
+// the next boots, and refuse that until the next boot.
+//
+#define SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_TRY_OTHER  9
+#define SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_LOCK       10
+
 /* Used by capsule updates as a standalone command or modifier to v2 commands */
 #define SMMSTORE_CMD_USE_FULL_FLASH  0x80
 
